==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|celtis||chisel}}, very probably a [[ghost word]] originating from a copyist's error in the Vulgate Bible, but taken as genuine and subsequently used in Medieval Latin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/sɛlt/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A prehistoric chisel-bladed tool.

