#: {{ux|lv|'''celt''' par priekšnieku|to make (lit. '''raise''') someone a chief|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|kas tad šos par ministriem '''cels''', ja ne mēs paši|who will make (lit. '''raise''', '''lift''') them ministers, if not we ourselves?|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''celt''' āzi par dārznieku|to '''raise''', to '''employ''' a goat as a gardener ({{=}} to give a position to someone who cannot be trusted, who will misuse it)|inline=1}}
# to [[make]] (someone) [[rise]], to [[awaken]], to [[wake up]] (also figuratively)
#: {{ux|lv|'''celt''' no rīta bērnus augšā|to '''wake up''' (lit. lift up(ward)) the children in the morning|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|rītos viņu '''ceļ''' gaiļa dziesma|in the morning the rooster's crow '''wakes''' him '''up'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|Lāčplēsis, diženais vīrs, latviešus cīniņā '''ceļ'''|the Bear Slayer, a great man, '''awakened''' the Latvians in ({{=}} to) the struggle|inline=1}}
# to [[build]], to [[construct]] (a house, a building, etc.)
#: {{ux|lv|'''celt''' namu, skolu, rūpnīcu|to '''build''' a house, a school, a factory|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''celt''' pieminekli|to '''build''' a monument|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|jauno tiltu '''cēla''' draugu, brāļu rokas|the hands of friends and brothers '''built''' the new bridge|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|Egles māja bija '''celta''' no sarkaniem ķieģeļiem|Egle's house was '''built''' of red bricks|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''celt''' gaisa pilis|to '''build''' air castles (i.e., to fantasize, to dream about impossible things)|inline=1}}
# {{lb|lv|figuratively}} to [[build]], to [[make]]
#: {{ux|lv|'''celt''' jauno dzīvi|to '''build''' a new life|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|jau šodien mēs '''ceļam''' rītdienu|already today we '''are building''' tomorrow|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|Kas pats zin atrast labu, ļaunu, / tas pasauli zin '''celt''' par jaunu|he who knows good from evil / can '''build''' the world anew|inline=1}}
# {{lb|lv|colloquial}} to [[raise]], to [[make]], to [[create]], to [[generate]]
#: {{ux|lv|'''celt''' troksni kā elli|to '''make''' noise like hell|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''celt''' traci, paniku|to '''raise''' (an) uproar, panic|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''celt''' kādam neslavu|to '''raise''' disrepute, infamy on someone ({{=}} to spread compromising information about someone)|inline=1}}
# {{lb|lv|of claims, complaints, objections, protest}} to [[raise]], to [[allege]]
#: {{ux|lv|pratināšanas sākumā izmeklētājs jautā apsūdzētajam, vai viņš atzīst sevi par vainīgu '''celtajā''' apsūdzībā|at the beginning of the interrogation the investigator asked the accused if he declared himself guilty of the '''alleged''' charges|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|amatpersonas, kurām piešķirta tiesība '''celt''' protestus, var apturēt attiecīgu spriedumu|officers who were granted the right '''to raise''' protests, can stop the corresponding trial|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|labākos kumosus, glītākās drēbes dabūja Dāvis... “viņš jau tāds slimīgs”,» aizstāvēja māte, kad Jūle ar Rūdi '''cēla''' iebildumus|Dāvis got the best bites (of food), the pretties clothes... “he is so sickly,” (his) mother defended him, when Jūle and Rūde '''raised''' objections|inline=1}}

